# Testing

## Unit and integration (Vitest)

- Runner: Vitest with TZ=UTC
- Configs: app/vitest.config.ts, app/vitest.config.coverage.ts, app/vitest.resolve-aliases.ts, app/vitest.setup.ts
- Typical command: pnpm test (from repo root delegates to app)
- CI sets minimal env (DATABASE_URL dummy, PLAID_CLIENT_ID/SECRET placeholders) and runs prisma generate before tests
- Coverage tasks available (test:coverage, coverage:view/report/open/serve helpers)

Key suites:
- server/api/__tests__ — broad endpoint coverage incl. auth, accounts, budgets, register entries, reoccurrences, reports, reconciliation, tasks, admin
- server/services/**/__tests__ — PlaidSyncService, TransactionMatchingService, HashService, JwtService, reconciliation, reports
- server/services/forecast/**/__tests__ — core forecast integration/regression/unit tests
- lib/__tests__ and schema/__tests__ — utilities, Zod behaviors

## Forecast engine testing

- Custom test runner: app/server/services/forecast/__tests__/test-runner.ts
- Commands:
  - pnpm test:forecast — quick functionality
  - pnpm test:forecast:unit — ModernCache unit tests
  - pnpm test:forecast:integration — integration tests
  - pnpm test:forecast:all — runs unit + integration + runner

## End-to-end (Playwright)

- Playwright config: app/playwright.config.ts
- Specs under app/tests/e2e/specs/{public,authed}
- Visual snapshots committed under ...visual.spec.ts-snapshots/
- Commands:
  - pnpm test:e2e — chromium-public and chromium-authed
  - pnpm test:e2e:update-snapshots — local baselines
  - pnpm test:e2e:update-snapshots:staging — baselines vs https://staging.dineros.cc
- CI includes a manual workflow (e2e-update-staging-snapshots.yml) to regenerate Linux PNG baselines vs staging

## Mocks and environment

- Tests run in Node with mocks; MySQL/Redis generally not required (CI uses a dummy DATABASE_URL and generates Prisma client)
- Crypto-specific tests can be run with pnpm test:crypto
